# Chroma library, modern Earth: THE SPHERES OF SOCIETY, gathering life moments. Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3 (chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; the list is
# character.moments in spheres-data/gather.json). Every moment carries sphere: gather, every option the face it acts in
# (a cross option X>Y the means colour's face; a pair option the wheel-order pair face, WR as .RW, WG as .GW, UG as .GU).
# Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: SPEC.md. Words for faces and places: earth_spheres.py (no face named by colour).
# Evenness: in every life event each one-colour option has chance 60 and each pair option 50; in every everyday moment
# each one-colour option 75 and each cross option 65; so each colour's mean is the same in every stage.
# Everyday pairs (one calls two colours, its partner the other three, same stages and ages): the keeper knows your name
# BG (s1) with heard first at the corner table WUR (s2); a seat kept for the neighbour who lives alone WUB (s3) with the
# song the room calls for RG (s4).
# Life events and their pair sets: the first night out at eighteen D3a, turned away at the door D4a, the toast at the
# wedding D6a, the old bar is sold D2a.
# Doors (gather.json character.doors) used as works: lines: a friend who becomes a partner (first night out), a tab
# from the host and a job heard of at the table (keeper knows your name, corner table), a movement's first meeting
# (corner table), a seat on the festival committee (seat kept), a stage on an open night (the song), taking on the old
# place (the old bar is sold).
# Skipped as already written: the year's great feast or fair ('the year's great gathering', ready/gathering); a fight
# to step into or away from ('a pub argument turns into a fight', earth.py); meeting someone across a crowded room
# ('falling in love' and 'someone asks you home after the party', earth.py); a wake for a regular ('the wake in the old
# bar', ready/ev-gather).

# ================================================================ the first night out (gather.night)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the first night out at eighteen (pairs D3a)

== the first night out at eighteen
tier: life event
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.night
ladder: newcomer
once: yes
stages: young_adult
age: 18-20
per_year: 0 0 .1 0 0 0
drivers: ties+.3 community+.2 money+.1
times: Most young people in towns with bars and clubs go out with friends once they reach the legal age; the first night out that stays in a life, remembered for who was there and how it went, comes to about 1 in 4 lives, once (estimate), set at 1 in 10 a year from 18 to 20
likelier: a town with a busy high street, a close group of school friends, a birthday on a weekend
rarer: a remote village, a family or faith that keeps from drink, no money to spare, a job on nights
gap: 10-30
tone: mixed
life: friends, play, love
horizon: moment
roles: friend, prospect
who: friend
earth: you are eighteen, and your friends take you out on the town for the first time: the queue, the door, the bar and the dance floor
scene: {N} has turned eighteen, and {friend} has planned the whole night: the corner bar first, then the club on the high street. There is a queue down the pavement, music through the wall, and the door staff are checking ages.
scene W: {N} has promised a text home at midnight, and promised {friend} that nobody gets left behind. Both promises feel bigger once the door opens.
scene U: {N} wants to see what the town is like after dark: who goes where, who knows whom, and how the night is run.
scene B: Half of {Ns} year from school will be inside. Tonight sets who {N} is to them for the next few years.
scene R: {N} has waited years for this. The music is loud, the night is long, and {N} means to be the last one off the floor.
scene G: {Ns} older cousins all had their first night out at the same bar on the corner, and the barman still asks after them.
- W | keep the group together all night, and see everyone home safe | v: benevolence, security | sphere: gather.W | chance: 60
- U | stay near the edge for the first hour, and watch how the place works | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 60
- B | make sure you are seen with the right crowd, and leave with their numbers | act: make sure they are seen with the right crowd, and leave with their numbers | v: power, achievement | sphere: gather.B | chance: 60
- R | dance from the first song until the lights come on | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 60
- G | start at the corner bar where your cousins started, and toast them there | act: start at the corner bar where their cousins started, and toast them there | v: tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 60
- WU | agree the plan with everyone first: one meeting place, one taxi, one time home | v: security, conformity | sphere: gather.WU | chance: 50
- WR | talk the door staff round when they stop the youngest of your group | act: talk the door staff round when they stop the youngest of their group | v: benevolence, stimulation | lever: voice | sphere: gather.RW | chance: 50
- UB | find out where the good crowd goes on which night, and follow it there | v: achievement, self-direction | sphere: gather.UB | chance: 50
- RG | leave the club at three with everyone, and watch the sun come up from the hill | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.RG | chance: 50
- BG | make one drink last all night, and get to know the barman instead | v: security, tradition | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 50
works: The night becomes the story the group tells for years, and by the end of it the barman knows {Ns} face.
works: {prospect}, met by the bar at midnight, asks for {Ns} number at the end of the night and calls the next day.
fails: {friend} is turned away at the door, the group splits up, and {N} spends the night looking for everyone.
fails: The drinks cost twice what {N} expected, and the night ends early, broke, in a cold taxi queue.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: turned away at the door (pairs D4a)

== turned away at the door
tier: life event
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.night
ladder: newcomer
stages: young_adult adult
age: 18-35
per_year: 0 0 .015 .006 0 0
drivers: harsh+.3 community-.2 ties+.1
times: Door staff at clubs and members' rooms turn people away for dress, age, the list or how they look; being turned away in front of friends, in a way that stings, comes to about 1 in 5 lives (estimate), set at 1.5 in 100 a year in the twenties and less after
likelier: a city with strict doors, a person who looks unlike the usual crowd, one friend in a group who does not fit the door, a smart venue
rarer: a small town with one bar where everyone knows the door, a person who rarely goes out
gap: 3-10
tone: trouble
life: friends, identity, play
horizon: moment
roles: friend, rival
who: friend
earth: the club door waves your friends in, then stops you: not tonight, not dressed like that, not on the list
scene: The queue moves, the door staff wave {friend} and the others through, and then a hand comes up in front of {N}. Not tonight. No reason is given, and the friends are already inside.
scene W: {N} has read the rules posted by the door and broken none of them. Being refused for nothing feels like being refused for who {N} is.
scene U: {N} looks at who was let in and who was not, and starts to see the pattern.
scene B: {rival} is just inside the door, watching. Whatever {N} does next will be talked about on Monday.
scene R: {Ns} face is hot. Every part of {N} wants to tell the doorman exactly what {N} thinks of him.
scene G: {N} thinks of the old bar on the corner where nobody has ever been turned away, and of the people there who would never do this.
- W | ask the doorman calmly which rule you broke, and wait for an answer | act: ask the doorman calmly which rule they broke, and wait for an answer | v: conformity, self-direction | lever: voice | sphere: gather.W | chance: 60
- U | watch the door for ten minutes, and work out whom it lets in and why | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: gather.U | chance: 60
- B | ring the friend of a friend who knows the manager, and get put on the list | v: power, achievement | sphere: gather.B | chance: 60
- R | tell the doorman what you think of him, loudly, and walk off down the street | act: tell the doorman what they think of him, loudly, and walk off down the street | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: exit | sphere: gather.R | chance: 60
- G | text the others to meet at the old corner bar, where everyone gets in | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: exit | sphere: gather.G | chance: 60
- WU | write a plain, fair account of the door, and ask who else it has happened to | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | sphere: gather.WU | chance: 50
- WB | come back next week in the right clothes, learn the doorman's name, and be let in | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: gather.WB | chance: 50
- UR | start an open night of your own in a cellar, with no list and no door | act: start an open night of their own in a cellar, with no list and no door | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 50
- RG | take the group to the park with music on a phone, and dance under the trees | v: hedonism, stimulation | tech: phone | sphere: gather.RG | chance: 50
- BG | shrug it off, and make a night of it at the late café by the market | v: security, hedonism | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 50
works: The others come out to join {N}, and the night that follows is better than the club would ever have been.
works: Word gets round, and the club changes its door within the month; {N} is let in, and finds it no longer matters much.
fails: The friends stay inside, and {N} goes home alone on the night bus, feeling small.
fails: The doorman remembers {Ns} face, and the door stays shut every time after.

# ================================================================ the haunt (gather.house)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls BG (cycle s1); partner: heard first at the corner table

== the keeper knows your name
tier: everyday
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.house
ladder: newcomer
stages: juvenile+
age: 16-100
calls: BG
rate: .5
share: .3
tone: joy
life: friends, community
horizon: months
roles: keeper, regular, friend
who: keeper
earth: after a few months of coming in, the café's keeper calls you by name and starts making your usual before you ask
times: Being known by name at a café, bar or club is the step from stranger to regular (Oldenburg 1989 on third places); most people who keep a haunt make it, and the moment it is felt and chosen comes to about 3 in 10 lives, once or twice (estimate). Earth's 'a seat at the regulars' table' is the later step, at sixty, into the regulars' own table
likelier: a small town, a person who goes to the same place at the same time, a keeper who has run the place for years
rarer: a big city of chain shops, a person who moves often, shift work
gap: 5-15
scene: For three months {N} has come in most mornings. Today the keeper looks up, says "{N}, the usual?" and starts making it before {N} reaches the counter. Two regulars at the window table nod.
scene W: Being known means being counted on. {N} notices that the jar by the till is for the keeper's daughter's school trip.
scene U: {N} has been listening for weeks, and knows now who the regulars are and what they argue about.
scene B: The regulars at the window table run half the businesses on the street. A nod from them is worth having.
scene R: {N} grins. It feels like being let in on a secret.
scene G: The keeper's mother ran the café before her, and {Ns} grandparents drank coffee here. It feels like coming home.
- W | put something in the jar, and offer to help when the keeper is short-handed | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | sphere: gather.W | chance: 75
- U | join the window table's argument about the news, and hold your own | act: join the window table's argument about the news, and hold their own | v: self-direction, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 75
- B | introduce yourself to each regular in turn, and remember what each one does | act: introduce themselves to each regular in turn, and remember what each one does | v: achievement, power | sphere: gather.B | chance: 75
- R | answer the keeper with a joke, and have the whole café laughing by nine | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 75
- G | come in at the same hour every day, and keep to the same seat | v: tradition, security | sphere: gather.G | chance: 75
- W>U | keep track of the regulars' troubles, and ask after each one the next morning | v: benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 65
- U>B | listen at the window table until you know who on the street needs what | act: listen at the window table until they know who on the street needs what | v: power, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 65
- B>R | buy the window table coffee on your birthday, and make a morning of it | act: buy the window table coffee on their birthday, and make a morning of it | v: hedonism, power | lever: fund | sphere: gather.B | chance: 65
- R>G | bring a cake on the café's anniversary, and get the whole room singing | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 65
- G>W | bring the keeper soup from home the week she is ill, as your family always did | act: bring the keeper soup from home the week she is ill, as their family always did | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 65
works: The café becomes {Ns} second home, and in a month when money is short the keeper quietly opens a tab.
works: A regular at the window table hears what {N} does, and mentions a job going two streets away.
fails: {N} says the wrong thing at the window table, and the nods turn into polite silence for a while.
fails: Being known cuts both ways: by the end of the week the whole street knows {Ns} business.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WUR (cycle s2); partner: the keeper knows your name

== heard first at the corner table
tier: everyday
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.house
ladder: regular
stages: juvenile+
age: 16-100
calls: WUR
rate: .5
share: .25
tone: mixed
life: community, work, friends
horizon: week
roles: regular, keeper, friend, grandparent
who: regular
earth: at the café's corner table a regular says the plant will close in the spring, days before it is in the news
times: News travels through haunts before it reaches print, and the regulars' table is often where a town hears first (Oldenburg 1989; the gather events news_sheet and rumour_runs are the world's versions); hearing big local news first at one's own haunt, and choosing what to do with it, comes to about 1 in 4 lives, a few times (estimate)
likelier: a regular at a busy café or bar, a small town with one big employer, a regular who works at the town hall or the plant
rarer: no regular haunt, a big city, a person who keeps to the phone
gap: 4-12
scene: At the corner table a regular who works in the plant's office lowers her voice: the plant will close in the spring, and four hundred jobs go with it. The papers have nothing yet, and half the table has family working there.
scene W: Some of the people at the table should hear this properly, from someone who cares, before they read it anywhere else.
scene U: {N} wants to know whether it is true. A whisper at a table has been wrong before.
scene B: News like this, a few days early, is worth something: a house to sell before prices fall, a job to look for first.
scene R: {N} is angry already. Four hundred families, and the people at the top kept it quiet.
scene G: {grandparent} worked at the plant, and so did half the street. {N} thinks of the families it has fed for three generations.
- W | tell the friends with family at the plant, quietly, before the papers do | v: benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 75
- U | ask who else has heard, and check it before passing on a word | v: universalism, security | sphere: gather.U | chance: 75
- B | keep it to yourself, and quietly start looking for work elsewhere | act: keep it to themselves, and quietly start looking for work elsewhere | v: security, achievement | sphere: gather.B | chance: 75
- R | ring the paper that afternoon, and let the whole town know | v: stimulation, universalism | lever: voice | sphere: gather.R | chance: 75
- G | go round to your grandparent's old workmates, and sit with them over it | act: go round to their grandparent's old workmates, and sit with them over it | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: gather.G | chance: 75
- W>B | ask the keeper for the back room, and call a meeting with the union there | v: conformity, power | lever: voice | sphere: gather.W | chance: 65
- U>R | find the plant's accounts online, and post what they really say | v: universalism, stimulation | tech: internet | sphere: gather.U | chance: 65
- B>G | tell the regulars who is hiring, so the street's own are first in line | v: benevolence, security | sphere: gather.B | chance: 65
- R>W | turn the table's anger into a march to the gates by Friday | v: stimulation, universalism | lever: voice | sphere: gather.R | chance: 65
- G>U | ask the oldest regulars what the town did the last time a works shut | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: gather.G | chance: 65
works: The table moves before anyone else in town, and the first meeting in the café's back room is where the campaign starts.
works: A regular hears of a job going in the next town, and {N} passes it to a friend in time.
fails: The whisper is wrong in half its details, and {N} is blamed for frightening the whole street.
fails: By the time {N} acts, the news is everywhere, and the chance to do anything first has gone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the old bar is sold (pairs D2a)

== the old bar is sold
tier: life event
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.house
ladder: regular
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-90
per_year: 0 0 .004 .004 .004 .004
drivers: prosper-.3 community-.2
times: Bars, cafés and clubs close often (a sale, the rent, the keeper retiring, a slow trade); having one's own regular haunt close comes to about 1 in 4 lives, once or twice (estimate), set at 4 in 1000 a year from 20
likelier: years as a regular at one place, a high street with rising rents, a keeper near retirement, hard times
rarer: no regular haunt, a busy place in a good year, a person who moves often and keeps no haunt
gap: 8-25
tone: trouble
life: friends, community, home
horizon: months
roles: keeper, regular, friend
who: keeper
earth: the bar you have gone to for years is sold to be turned into flats, and the last night is on Saturday
scene: The notice is taped to the bar's door: the building is sold, and the last night is Saturday. The keeper is pouring as usual, but nobody at the long table knows where they will go on Monday.
scene W: Thirty people sit at this table each week, and some of them have nowhere else. {N} thinks of them first.
scene U: {N} wants to know who bought it, for how much, and whether anything can still be done.
scene B: The keeper is retiring, not ruined. With the right backers, someone could take on the licence somewhere new.
scene R: {N} is not ready to let it go quietly. If it must end, it should end with the best night it has ever had.
scene G: {Ns} name is cut into the long table, beside names from fifty years ago. The table, at least, should not go in a skip.
- W | make a list of every regular, and find each one a table somewhere new | v: benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 60
- U | look up the sale at the council, and find out whether it can be stopped | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | sphere: gather.U | chance: 60
- B | ask the keeper about taking on the licence, and find two backers by Saturday | v: achievement, power | lever: lead | sphere: gather.B | chance: 60
- R | plan the loudest last night the street has heard, with a band and a midnight toast | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 60
- G | ask the buyers for the long table, and carry it home with the regulars | v: tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 60
- WU | call a meeting of the regulars, and put to a vote where the group goes next | v: conformity, universalism | lever: voice | sphere: gather.WU | chance: 50
- WG | move the Thursday table, rota and all, to the café across the road | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | sphere: gather.GW | chance: 50
- UR | put on a night of stories about the old place, and record every one | v: universalism, stimulation | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 50
- BR | buy the old sign, and hang it over a back room you rent yourself | act: buy the old sign, and hang it over a back room they rent themselves | v: self-direction, power | lever: found | sphere: gather.BR | chance: 50
- BG | let it go, and become a regular at the next nearest bar within the month | v: security | lever: exit | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 50
works: Most of the regulars follow {N} to the new place, and within a season the long table is full again.
works: {N} ends up behind a bar of {Ns} own, with the old sign over the door and the old keeper as the first customer.
fails: The last night ends, the group scatters, and some of the regulars are not seen out again.
fails: The new place never feels the same, and {N} stops going out on Thursdays at all.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WUB (cycle s3); partner: the song the room calls for

== a seat kept for the neighbour who lives alone
tier: everyday
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.house
ladder: regular
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-100
calls: WUB
rate: .5
share: .2
tone: mixed
life: neighbours, community, friends
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, keeper, regular, grandparent
who: neighbour
earth: the widower next door has not been out since the funeral, and you could bring him to your table at the café on Thursdays
times: Loneliness after a loss or in old age is common, and an invitation from a neighbour to a regular table is one known way back (Holt-Lunstad 2010 on social ties; Klinenberg 2002); keeping a seat for a lonely neighbour at one's haunt comes to about 1 in 5 lives, once or twice (estimate)
likelier: a street with many old people, a regular haunt of one's own, a neighbour lately widowed or retired
rarer: no regular haunt, a street of short lets, a person who does not know the neighbours
gap: 5-15
scene: Since the funeral in the spring, the widower next door has hardly left the house. On Thursday nights {N} goes to the café's long table, and there is always a spare chair.
scene W: Nobody on the street should sit alone every evening while there is a chair free. {N} feels it as plain duty.
scene U: {N} wonders what he would actually like. Not everyone wants a crowd after a loss.
scene B: Bringing him means minding him all evening, and the regulars may not take to him. It is a cost, and {N} knows it.
scene R: {N} would rather knock and drag him out tonight than think about it any longer.
scene G: In {Ns} grandparents' day, the street fed its widowers on a rota. {N} misses that.
- W | knock on his door, and ask him to the Thursday table | v: benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 75
- U | ask him what he used to enjoy, and find the place that fits it | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 75
- B | mention him to the keeper, and let the café do the inviting | v: security | sphere: gather.B | chance: 75
- R | turn up at his door at seven with his coat, and refuse to go without him | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: gather.R | chance: 75
- G | keep a chair at the table with his name on it, every Thursday, until he comes | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | sphere: gather.G | chance: 75
- W>R | get the whole table to sign a card asking him to the next birthday night | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: gather.W | chance: 65
- U>G | find out which dish his late wife made, and ask the keeper to cook it | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: gather.U | chance: 65
- B>W | ask him to keep the tally at quiz night, so he has a job there | v: benevolence, power | sphere: gather.B | chance: 65
- R>U | take him to the quiz, and put him on your team for the history round | act: take him to the quiz, and put him on their team for the history round | v: stimulation, universalism | sphere: gather.R | chance: 65
- G>B | introduce him to the old regulars from his own trade, who could use his help | v: tradition, achievement | sphere: gather.G | chance: 65
works: By the autumn he is at the table before {N} is, and he is the one keeping a seat for the next newcomer.
works: The table takes him in, and the next year he sits on the committee of the street's summer festival.
fails: He comes once, sits in silence, and does not answer the door the next Thursday.
fails: One regular makes it plain he is not welcome, and {N} has to choose between them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls RG (cycle s4); partner: a seat kept for the neighbour who lives alone

== the song the room calls for
tier: everyday
sphere: gather
haunt: gather.house
ladder: regular
stages: young_adult+
age: 18-100
calls: RG
rate: .5
share: .2
tone: joy
life: friends, play, community
horizon: months
roles: regular, keeper, friend, grandparent
who: regular
earth: one night at the bar you sing an old song for a dare, and now the regulars call for it every time you walk in
times: Regulars at bars and clubs often have a song, a party piece or a nickname the room gives them (Oldenburg 1989; Finnegan 1989 on the town's hidden music-makers); a song that becomes one's own at a haunt comes to about 1 in 5 lives (estimate)
likelier: a bar with music nights, a person who sings or plays, a close crowd of regulars
rarer: no regular haunt, a quiet café crowd, a person who never sings in public
gap: 5-20
scene: One night at the bar {N} sang an old song for a dare, badly and with feeling, and the whole room joined the chorus. Now whenever {N} walks in, someone at the back starts the first line.
scene W: The song has become part of the evening, and the regulars count on it. {N} feels bound to give it its due.
scene U: {N} has started looking up where the song came from, and what the verses nobody sings are about.
scene B: The keeper says a song night with {N} at the front would fill the room on Tuesdays. There might be something in it.
scene R: {N} loves it: the shout from the back, the whole room on the chorus, the roar at the end.
scene G: It was {Ns} grandparent's song first. Every time the room sings it, a little of the old house comes back.
