- U | learn the lost verses, and sing them the next time the room calls | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: gather.U | chance: 75
- B | agree to the keeper's song night, for a share of the takings | v: achievement, power | sphere: gather.B | chance: 75
- R | stand on a chair and sing it with everything you have | act: stand on a chair and sing it with everything they have | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 75
- G | tell the room it was your grandparent's song, and sing it in their memory | act: tell the room it was their grandparent's song, and sing it in that memory | v: tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 75
- W>G | teach the chorus to the newest regulars, so the song stays with the room | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 65
- U>W | write the words out and pin them by the bar, so anyone can join in | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: gather.U | chance: 65
- B>U | record the room singing it, and send it to the regulars who moved away | v: achievement, benevolence | tech: phone | sphere: gather.B | chance: 65
- R>B | take the song to the open night across town, and win that room too | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 65
- G>R | bring your grandparent's old fiddle, and play the tune for the room | act: bring their grandparent's old fiddle, and play the tune for the room | v: tradition, hedonism | sphere: gather.G | chance: 65
works: The song becomes {Ns} for good, and years later strangers ask the keeper which of the regulars is the one who sings it.
works: The keeper gives {N} the stage on the open night, and the room is full by eight.
fails: The joke wears thin, and some nights {N} would rather sit in peace than be called up again.
fails: One night {N} forgets the words in front of a full room, and a laugh from the back carries.

# ================================================================ the toast (a wedding)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the toast at the wedding (pairs D6a)

== the toast at the wedding
tier: life event
sphere: gather
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 22-64
per_year: 0 0 .006 .008 .004 0
drivers: ties+.3 family+.2 community+.1
times: Most weddings have a toast or a speech by a friend or relative of the couple; being asked to give one comes to about 1 in 4 lives, once or twice (estimate), set at under 1 in 100 a year from the twenties to the forties. Earth's 'a friend's wedding' and 'dancing at a wedding' are the guest's moments; this is the one asked to speak
likelier: a close friend or sibling marrying, a person known to be good with words, a large circle of friends
rarer: few friends marrying, a family without the custom of toasts, a person known to be shy
gap: 4-15
tone: mixed
life: friends, love, family
horizon: week
roles: friend
who: friend
earth: your oldest friend is getting married, and has asked you to give the toast in front of two hundred guests
scene: {friend} is getting married on Saturday and has asked {N} to give the toast. There will be two hundred guests and a microphone, and {N} has a folder of old stories, some of which should never be told in front of a grandmother.
scene W: A toast is a promise said aloud for the couple. {N} wants every word to honour them and leave nobody out.
scene U: {N} has drafted it four times, looking for the one true thing about {friend} that everyone in the room will recognise.
scene B: Half the guests are people {N} would like to know better. A good toast could open doors for years.
scene R: {N} cannot plan it. It will come out on the night, from the heart, or not at all.
scene G: {N} has known {friend} since they were small. The toast should be about the street they grew up on and the families in the room.
- W | name everyone who helped the couple, and leave nobody out | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: gather.W | chance: 60
- U | write it out, try it on three friends, and cut every line that rings false | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 60
- B | keep it short, polished and funny, and work the right tables afterwards | v: achievement, power | sphere: gather.B | chance: 60
- R | throw away the notes, and say what you feel about your friend | act: throw away the notes, and say what they feel about their friend | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: gather.R | chance: 60
- G | tell the story of the two families, and raise a glass to the grandparents | v: tradition | sphere: gather.G | chance: 60
- BG | tell the one embarrassing story everyone knows anyway, and let the room laugh along | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: gather.BG | chance: 50
- UG | ask the couple's grandparents how they met, and build the toast round it | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: gather.GU | chance: 50
- UR | write a short funny poem about the couple, and lead the room in its last line | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: gather.UR | chance: 50
- WB | toast the couple, thank the hosts and the cooks, and pass the hat for the honeymoon | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | sphere: gather.WB | chance: 50
- WR | call the couple's oldest friends to their feet to raise their glasses together | v: benevolence, stimulation | sphere: gather.RW | chance: 50
works: The hall laughs in the right places and goes quiet in the right one, and {friend} holds {N} hard at the end.
works: For years afterwards {N} is asked to say a few words at every wedding, and strangers remember {N} as the one who gave that toast.
fails: The microphone squeals, a joke falls flat, and {N} sits down to polite clapping and a hot face.
fails: One story goes too far, a grandmother stops smiling, and {friend} is cool with {N} for a month.
